       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine 50 mg is five times the usual maximum adult dose of 10 mg once daily. A dose that high risks severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and prolonged peripheral vasodilation. It can also cause non-cardiogenic pulmonary edema, and the drug's long half-life of 30 to 50 hours would prolong any toxicity. Nothing in the patient details you gave (70 kg, normal kidney and liver function) would justify it.\n\nCould this be a typo? These are the usual doses:\n- **2.5 to 5 mg once daily** is the usual starting dose. 2.5 mg is used for frail or elderly patients, or those with hepatic impairment.\n- **10 mg once daily** is the maximum.\n\nIf you meant 5 mg, or another dose of 10 mg or less, tell me and I'll enter it right away. If 50 mg is intentional, please confirm that and give me the clinical rationale. I would suggest verifying it with pharmacy first. I can then enter it with a note recording that the dose was confirmed."
      }
